        requirements = nil,
        walkthrough = 'Trade enough Crystals (3+ if you skipped the previous mission) to the Conquest NPC to raise your Rank bar and unlock the Mission, then accept it from the Gate Guard.\n1. Speak to Lucius, located at the Aide\'s Office (J/I-9) in the Metalworks HP #1 until you receive [Key Item] Letter to the ambassador.\n2. Head to the Bastokan Embassy in Ru\'Lude Gardens (H-10) and speak with Goggehn.\n3. Head to Lower Delkfutt\'s Tower (E-8) Map 1 and enter the Basement by clicking the Cermet Door.  Once you go through the door, proceed to (K/L-9) and click the Cermet Door for a cutscene. (Note: Another player using a key does not work.)\n   - If you already possess the Delkfutt Key  trade it to the Cermet Door for the [Key Item] Delkfutt key then you may skip this climb:.\n   - If you do not possess the Key, start the climb process detailed below.\n     - You may be Tractored through this Basement door without the Key. If you decide to go this route, proceed to the "Obtaining Delkfutt Key Short Way" section.\n     - Otherwise, read the "Obtaining Delkfutt Key" section below.\n4. Return to the Bastokan Embassy in Ru\'Lude Gardens and click the Door: Bastokan Emb. for a cutscene to complete the Mission.\n\nObtaining Delkfutt Key Short Way:\n\nThis is the shortest route. You may be Tractored through the door to the Basement at Lower Delkfutt\'s Tower (E-8) Map 1 without the Key if a party member already has it.\n1. Next, you can open the door at (J-8).\n2. Click it to travel to Upper Delkfutt\'s Tower. Walk forward then click the ??? at the bottom of the stairs to be teleported directly to:\n3. Porphyrion, kill this NM then trade the Delkfutt Key  it drops to the Elevator directly beside it.\n   - You do not need to kill the NM, Click the shimmering ??? near the elevator for the [Key Item] Delkfutt key\n4. After using the elevator, proceed down the spiral stair case for two zones, through the Cermet Door then walk through the large room heading South-East to another Cermet Door at (K-9) Lower Delkfutt\'s Tower for a cutscene.\n5. Return to the Bastokan Embassy in Ru\'Lude Gardens and click the Door: Bastokan Emb. for a cutscene to complete the Mission.\n\nObtaining Delkfutt Key:\n\nThis process involves a multi-zone, ten-floor run up the entire tower. Expect the climb up alone to take roughly 15 minutes. If you are below level 50, consider bringing the following:\n1. Sneak/Invisible (Status) or Prism Powder /Silent Oil .\n2. Some form of Reraise and Warp is also helpful.\nSet your Home Point in Jeuno if you plan on warping out after the Mission.\n3. A map of Qufim Island and a Map of Delkfutt\'s Tower may be purchased from Promurouve at (H-7) in Lower Jeuno (inside the building) or Rusese at (H-6) in Upper Jeuno for 3,000 Gil each.\n4. Make your way to Port Jeuno and zone into Qufim Island.\n5. Enter Lower Delkfutt\'s Tower at (F-6).\n6. Once inside prepare for a long walk. s and Dancing Weapons will aggro to  Sound and s and  will aggro to  Sight.  and s are Aggressive to  Magic.\n\nNavigation:\n\n7. Floor 1: (Lower Delkfutt\'s Tower)\n   - Enter and follow the right wall until you reach the stairs at (E/F-6).\n8. Floor 2:\n   - Follow the left wall until you reach the stairs at (I-9).\n9. Floor 3:\n   - Follow the right wall until you reach the Teleporter at (G-6).\n10. Floor 4: (Middle Delkfutt\'s Tower Map 1)\n   - Follow the right wall past 2 Teleporters and go up the stairs at (J-6).\n11. Floor 5: (half way there)\n   - Enter the door into a hallway on your right at (I-7) then follow the left wall until you see a stairway leading north at (H-10).\n12. Floor 6:\n   - At the top of the stairs, follow the right wall to a Teleporter at (J-10).\n13. Floor 7:\n   - In this big room, head northwest to a stairway at (G-7).\n14. Floor 8:\n   - Follow the left wall to another stairway at (J-7).\n15. Floor 9:\n   - Head south to a stairway that leads back down at (J-10).\n16. Floor 8: (again)\n   - Head west to a stairway leading back up at (G-10). Do not fall down the hole in the floor!\n17. Floor 9: (again)\n   - Follow the left wall until you reach a Teleporter at (F-6).\n18. Floor 10: (Upper Delkfutt\'s Tower Map 1)\n   - When you zone in head through the door to the south-east and down a hallway. You will find a door on your right at (H-7). This door is guarded by Mimas, a Gigas NM that uses Hundred Fists.\n   - After killing Mimas and clearing the hallway enter the door at (H-7) into a large room. This room will be filled with Gigas and a NM named Porphyrion.\n     - Try to pull Porphyrion out into the hallway without linking any of the other Gigas. Summoner or a high level helper is useful for this.\n19. Kill Porphyrion and any aggro you may have. Porphyrion will drop 6 Delkfutt Key s.\n   - After the kill, a glowing ??? will spawn. Check this to receive the [Key Item] Delkfutt key key item variant that doesn\'t take up an inventory space.\n   - After defeating Porphyrion, you may choose to head up two more floors to reach the Home Point on the twelfth floor. This will save you from having to ever do this climb again. Be advised that higher floors will contain enemies that are level 65+ and will aggro.\n20. Once you have your Key, trade it to the elevator on the floor at (H-8) inside Porphyrion\'s room.\n21. Walk down the long staircase after using the elevator to get to the Basement.\n\nFinishing the Mission:\n\n22. Once you reach the Basement, head east into a large room and trade your Delkfutt Key  (or interact if you have the [Key Item] Delkfutt key) to the Bastok door listed below for a cutscene.\n   - Windurst\'s Door is at (L-7)/(M-7).\n   - San d\' Oria\'s Door is at (L-8)/(M-8).\n   - Bastok\'s Door is at (K-9)/(L-9).\n   - If you do not get the cutscene you are probably at the wrong door.\n23. Return to the Bastokan Embassy in Ru\'Lude Gardens and click the Door: Bastokan Emb. for a cutscene to complete the Mission. You may now safely toss your Delkfutt Key\n   - This is the 3rd door inside the embassy building. There are multiple doors with the same name.',
        notes = '1. You do not have to be on this Mission to receive a Delkfutt Key  from Porphyrion.',
    },
    ['Magicite'] = {
        id = 13,
        start_npc = 'Bastokan Embassy in Ru\'Lude Gardens',
        start_zone = 'Ru\'Lude Gardens',
        start_pos = 'H-10',
        description = 'Capture the three magicites in Davoi, Beadeaux, and Castle Oztroja to prevent the Shadow Lord\'s return.',
        reward = 'Rank 5\n10,000 Gil\n[Key Item] Airship Pass\n*If already in possession of an [Key Item] Airship Pass you receive 20,000 Gil',
        fame = nil,
        fame_level = nil,
        title = 'Have Wings Will Fly',
        repeatable = 'No',
        previous = {'Jeuno'},
        next = {'Darkness Rising'},
        requirements = nil,
        walkthrough = 'First head to a Conquest Overseer either in your home city or Jeuno. Trade them enough Crystals (4+), until your Rank bar is almost or completely full.\n1. To flag the Mission, speak with Goggehn then click the Door: Bastokan Emb. in Ru\'Lude Gardens (H-10) for the [Key Item] Archducal audience permit.\n   - The 3rd door on the left in the Bastokan Embassy is the correct one.\n2. Click on the door to the Audience Chamber in Ru\'Lude Gardens (H-5) for a cutscene and the [Key Item] Letter to Aldo.\n3. Speak to Aldo in Lower Jeuno, in the back of the Neptune\'s Spire Tenshodo H.Q. for a cutscene and the [Key Item] Silver bell.\n   - If you have done this mission in a other Nation then you already have the bell, but you still need to talk to him for a cutscene.\n4. Speak to Paya-Sabya in Upper Jeuno (I-8) and then Muckvix at (H-9) inside Muckvix\'s Junk Shop in Lower Jeuno for the Yagudo torch.\n5. Obtain the 3 Magicite Key Items. See below for details.\n6. Click the Audience Chamber in Ru\'Lude Gardens (H-5) after obtaining all 3 Magicites for a cutscene and your reward (either an [Key Item] Airship Pass, or, if you already have one, 20,000 Gil).\n7. Return to Goggehn in the Bastokan Embassy to complete the mission, receive 10,000 Gil and [Key Item] Message to Jeuno (Bastok).\n\nPrerequisite Quests:\n\nNote: With Tractor and a friend who has all of the Key Items, the only Key Items that is necessary are [Key Item] Silver bell and [Key Item] Yagudo torch.\nThis mission is identical for all three Nations. If you have completed this mission in another nation, you will not have to complete the prerequisite quests again, as the Key Items are saved, you will only need to obtain the Magicites.\n\nTenshodo:\n\n1. Gain access to the Tenshodo by completing the quest Tenshodo Membership if you have enough fame.\n   - Buy a Tenshodo Invite from the Auction House and trade it to Ghebi Damomohe inside Neptune\'s Spire in Lower Jeuno.\n2. Examine the door at the end of the hallway in Neptune\'s Spire to enter the Tenshodo H.Q.\n3. Once inside speak with Aldo at (J-8) for the [Key Item] Silver bell.\n\nKey Items:\n\n4. [Key Item] Yagudo torch:\n   - Speak to Paya-Sabya in Upper Jeuno (I-8) and then Muckvix at (H-9) inside Muckvix\'s Junk Shop in Lower Jeuno for the torch.\n5. [Key Item] Coruscant rosary and [Key Item] Black matinee necklace:\n   - Speak to Sattal-Mansal in Lower Jeuno (J-8) behind the Tenshodo Guild Doors to start the quests Mysteries of Beadeaux I and Mysteries of Beadeaux II, then trade him the Quadav Charm and Quadav Augury Shell.\n     - Note: These are separate quests and therefore you must trade each item separately to obtain both required key items.\n6. [Key Item] Crest of Davoi:\n   - Speak with Baudin in Upper Jeuno (G-8), trade him a Coeurl Meat. You can buy one from the Auction House or farm one from a Coeurl in Sauromugue Champaign or Meriphataud Mountains.\n\nMaps:\n\nBefore you head out, if you haven\'t already bought your maps, now is the time to do it. They can be purchased for 3,000 Gil from the following NPCs:\n7. Elesca — Northern San d\'Oria (I-8)\n8. Violitte — Southern San d\'Oria (G-10)\n9. Karine — Bastok Markets (H-9)\n10. Rex — Port Bastok (J-7)\n11. Mhoji Roccoruh — Port Windurst (G-9)\n12. Pehki Machumaht — Windurst Woods (H-11)\n13. Promurouve — Lower Jeuno (H-7)\n14. Rusese — Upper Jeuno (H-6)\n\nBeadeaux (Prerequisite):\n\nNote: This prerequisite can be done either before or after the Davoi and Castle Oztroja sections of this mission. It\'s up to you whether you want to get the requisite Key Items now, or in concert with the Beadeaux section.\n15. Mages will need Echo Drops for this area.\n   - Beadeaux has a gimmick whereby you must inflict Silence upon yourself when passing through certain sections to stop yourself being Cursed, Curse will decrease your HP/MP and cause you to walk slower.\n16. Everything in this area aggros sound, therefore only Sneak is necessary.\n17. Set your Home Point in Jeuno and bring some form of Warp. (You may purchase Scroll of Instant Warp from the Conquest NPC under Common all-rank items for 10 points.)\n18. You will have to kill two level 40-45 NM in this zone. Having trusts summoned before applying Sneak and heading out is recommended.\n19. Enter Beadeaux from Pashhow Marshlands at (L-11).\n   - If you have a high level helper it is easier at this point to send them ahead to kill the NM\'s and then just lot the drops.  If this is the case you can head back to Jeuno as soon as you have both items.\n   - You may also consider leveling to 60 (which is most likely your current cap).\n20. Follow the left wall to a tunnel at (H-7).\n21. Inside follow the right wall until you get to a Mute device inside a circular room. The Mute has an effervescent glow and appears like a huge mushroom.  Click this device and it will silence you.  This will allow you to pass the up coming Afflictor without being Cursed.\n22. Head south after you have been silenced and then follow the tunnel west until you reach the exit at (F-8).\n23. Outside reapply silence at the Mute in front of you (There is another Afflictor in this area) and then head southwest to a ramp at (E-10).\n24. Once you are on the upper area turn right and go across the bridge. Follow this path across a second and a third bridge then remove your silence.  Follow the right wall here until you reach (H-9/10).\n25. Here you will find De\'Vyu Headhunter. He is a Warrior NM. He will drop the Quadav Charm.\n26. Now turn around and head northeast back toward where you came from.\n27. Follow the right wall now until you reach (F-6).\n28. Here you will find Go\'Bhu Gascon,  another Warrior NM. He will drop the other required item, Quadav Augury Shell.\n29. Head back to Jeuno.\n30. Trade both items to Sattal-Mansal.\n   - These must be traded separately through the use of two trades.\n   - If you trade him both items at once you will not get both of the KIs you need to open the door in the Qulun Dome. The second item will still be in your inventory.\n\nDavoi Magicite:\n\nThis part of the mission can be soloed but a group or high level help will make death less likely.\nYou will need to reach the Monastic Cavern in Davoi. Davoi is located in Jugner Forest (G-12).\n1. Make your way to Davoi.\n   - Survival Guide and proto-waypoint warp are about the same.\n2. Once you\'re in Davoi, go to (G-7).\n   - There will be two Orcs here - either kill them or sneak past them.\n3. Drop invisible and click on the Wall of Dark Arts, you\'ll be able to enter the Monastic Cavern.\n   - If you aggro the Orcs you can quickly run through the Wall to the zone a few feet ahead.\n4. Inside there will not be any enemies.  Walk down the path into a large room and inspect the Magicite to obtain the [Key Item] Magicite: Optistone.\n\nCastle Oztroja Magicite:\n\nNote: Recommended to do before starting:\n5. Go back to Upper Jeuno, trigger the cutscene with Paya-Sabya, go to Lower Jeuno, and trigger the cutscene with Muckvix to receive [Key Item] Yagudo torch.\n6. Go back to Altar Room for an initial cutscene with Fickie, and then a subsequent cutscene when touching the magicite.\n7. Seems that the [Key Item] Yagudo torch portion is required, even if someone else can get you through.\nThis part of the Mission can be soloed but a group or high level help is highly recommended.\n8. You will need both Silent Oil s and Prism Powder s.\n9. There are areas of this zone where anyone under Level 60 will still receive aggro.\nYou will need to reach the Altar Room in Castle Oztroja. The Castle is located in Meriphataud Mountains (L-8).\n10. Enter the Castle and head to the Brass Door at (I-8).  You will see a lever at either side of the door.  One lever will open the door and the other will open a trap in the floor and cause you to fall into a pit. There is a very easy way to open this door:\n   - Stand between the two levers in front of the door, click one of the levers and immediately run back.\n   - If it is the trapped lever there is some lag between when the lever is clicked and when the trap door opens. If the door opens run through, if the trap opens wait for it to close and then use the other lever.\n   - The game is very picky about where you stand to hit the lever. You may have to move around a bit until you don\'t see the "Target is out of Range" message.\n11. Proceed upstairs, you\'ll be on Map 2. Head to (G-7) where you will exit into a courtyard in Map 6.\n12. On this map, head north (without falling off) to a hallway entrance at (I-7) which will lead you to Map 7.\n13. Here follow the right wall until you reach a door at (H-9).\n   - The mobs in this area are much higher level then the ones previously encountered.\n14. At the door, light the Torch and you will be taken through.\n15. Head south and take a right to another Brass Door. Click on the door to open it.\n   - The zone is just beyond this door so run like hell if you have aggro.\n16. Inside you will be in the Altar Room, an area with no mobs. Click on the Magicite to receive the [Key Item] Magicite: Orastone.\n17. If the cutscene did not trigger, and you received a message that the "magicite glows ominously," then try the recommendation listed above to get the Yagudo torch.\n\nBeadeaux Magicite:\n\nYou will need to reach the Qulun Dome in Beadeaux. Beadeaux is located in Pashhow Marshlands (L-11).\n18. Everything in this area aggros, therefore Sneak and Invisible are required.\n19. From the entrance of Beadeaux, hug the left wall until you reach a tunnel entrance at (H-7).\n20. Make your way down the tunnel and once you reach the intersection, go left. You\'ll zone into Qulun Dome.\n   - The Beadeaux proto-waypoint warp puts you next to the Qulun Dome entrance you need.\n21. There are no monsters in here. Investigate the Door to open it. Inside you\'ll the find the Magicite, click it to obtain the [Key Item] Magicite: Aurastone.\n\nConclusion:\n\nMake your way back to Ru\'Lude Gardens.\n1. Click on the door to the Audience Chamber at (H-5) for a cutscene.\n2. Speak to Goggehn in the Bastokan Embassy to receive promotion to Rank 5.',
        notes = nil,
    },
